{"id":757,"slug":"the-two-of-us","title":"The Two of Us","year":1967,"country":"France","duration":87,"spine":388,"url":"https://www.criterion.com/films/757-the-two-of-us","cover":"https://s3.amazonaws.com/criterion-production/films/ca4f48ae17ceaa8668b66f93cfecf246/Hf8BEOHsnzVLv22NbylOz1y27NVwQ8_large.jpg","description":"A young Jewish boy living in Nazi-occupied Paris is sent by his parents to the countryside to live with an elderly Catholic couple until France's liberation. Forced to hide his identity, the eight-year-old, Claude (played delicately by first-time actor Alain Cohen), bonds with the irascible, staunchly anti-Semitic Grampa (Michel Simon), who improbably becomes his friend and confidant. Poignant and lighthearted, The Two of Us was acclaimed director Claude Berri's debut feature, based on own childhood experiences, and gave the legendary Simon one of his most memorable roles in the twilight of his career. ","boxset":0,"scraped":1,"directors":[{"name":"Claude Berri","slug":"claude-berri"}],"cast":[{"actor":"Michel Simon","role":"Grampa","slug":"michel-simon"},{"actor":"Alain Cohen","role":"Claude Langmann","slug":"alain-cohen"},{"actor":"Charles Denner","role":"Mr. Langmann","slug":"charles-denner"},{"actor":"Luce Fabiole","role":"Grandma","slug":"luce-fabiole"},{"actor":"Roger Carel","role":"Victor","slug":"roger-carel"},{"actor":"Paul Prébois","role":"Maxime","slug":"paul-prebois"},{"actor":"Jacqueline Rouillard","role":"Schoolteacher","slug":"jacqueline-rouillard"},{"actor":"Marco Perrin","role":"Priest","slug":"marco-perrin"}],"credits":[{"role":"Director","person":"Claude Berri","slug":"claude-berri"},{"role":"Screenplay","person":"Claude Berri","slug":"claude-berri"},{"role":"Screenplay","person":"Gérard Brach","slug":null},{"role":"Screenplay","person":"Michel Rivelin","slug":null},{"role":"Producer","person":"André Hunebelle","slug":null},{"role":"Producer","person":"Paul Cadéac","slug":null},{"role":"Music","person":"Georges Delerue","slug":nul